### Best Practices

- Keep `modelValue` as a stable array ordered exactly like `columns`; sparse arrays are normalized, but explicit values make form state easier to audit.
- Provide `column.key` whenever columns can be reordered or conditionally rendered, so Vue does not reuse scroll containers for different data.
- Keep option `value` primitives stable. Store display names in `label`, not in the persisted value.
- Use inline mode (`popup=false`) for settings panels that should remain visible; use popup mode for mobile or task-focused transient choices.
- Do not put selectable disabled values in submitted form state. The component skips disabled options only when it has to normalize or recover from scroll.
- Keep `visibleItemCount` odd in design specs. The runtime rounds even numbers upward, which can make screenshots differ by one row.

## API Reference

### Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|------|
| `modelValue` | `PickerValue` | `[]` | Selected value per column. Missing, invalid, or non-array values normalize to the first enabled option. |
| `columns` | `PickerColumn[]` | `[]` | Column definitions rendered from left to right. |
| `visible` | `boolean` | `false` | Popup open state controlled by `v-model:visible`. |
| `popup` | `boolean` | `true` | Renders as a Teleport bottom popup when true; renders inline when false. |
| `title` | `string` | `''` | Center title shown in the toolbar. |
| `showToolbar` | `boolean` | `true` | Shows cancel/title/confirm toolbar actions. |
| `confirmText` | `string` | `'Confirm'` | Text for the confirm button. |
| `cancelText` | `string` | `'Cancel'` | Text for the cancel button. |
| `disabled` | `boolean` | `false` | Disables toolbar buttons, option buttons, and drag state updates. |
| `itemHeight` | `number` | `36` | Option row height in pixels; values below 24 are clamped to 24. |
| `visibleItemCount` | `number` | `5` | Number of visible rows. Even values are rounded up to the next odd count, with a minimum of 3. |
| `closeOnClickMask` | `boolean` | `true` | Closes the popup when the mask is clicked. |
| `lazyMount` | `boolean` | `true` | Delays popup body rendering until the picker has opened once. |

### PickerValue

```ts
type PickerValue = Array<string | number>
```

### PickerColumn

| Field | Type | Description |
|------|------|------|
| `key` | `string` | Optional stable key for the column. |
| `options` | `PickerOption[]` | Options available in this column. |

### PickerOption

| Field | Type | Description |
|------|------|------|
| `value` | `string \| number` | Primitive value emitted for the column. |
| `label` | `string` | Visible option label. |
| `disabled` | `boolean` | Prevents selecting this option and skips it during normalization fallback. |

### Events

| Event | Params | Description |
|------|------|------|
| `update:modelValue` | `(value: PickerValue)` | Emitted when scrolling changes a column value. |
| `change` | `(value: PickerValue)` | Emitted with the same normalized value after a live column change. |
| `update:visible` | `(visible: boolean)` | Popup visibility update emitted by open/close actions. |
| `confirm` | `(value: PickerValue)` | Emitted with the current local value when confirm is clicked, then closes. |
| `cancel` | - | Emitted when cancel is clicked, then closes. |
| `open` | - | Emitted when the picker opens. |
| `close` | - | Emitted when the picker closes. |

### Exposes

| Name | Type | Description |
|------|------|------|
| `open` | `() => void` | Opens the picker popup by writing `visible=true`. |
| `close` | `() => void` | Closes the picker popup. |
| `toggle` | `() => void` | Toggles the popup open state. |

## Slots

`TxPicker` does not expose slots. Use `columns[].options[].label` for visible option text and `title` / `confirmText` / `cancelText` for toolbar copy.

## Overview

- `modelValue` is always an array with one primitive value per column.
- Missing, invalid, or non-array model values normalize to the first enabled option in each column.
- Disabled options cannot be selected and are skipped by normalization fallback.
- Popup mode is controlled by `visible` / `v-model:visible`; inline mode renders immediately when `popup` is `false`.
- `visibleItemCount` is rounded up to an odd number and never below `3`; `itemHeight` is clamped to at least `24`.
- Scrolling emits `update:modelValue` and `change`; clicking confirm emits `confirm` with the current normalized value and then closes.
- A column is a drum the component turns itself, not a native scroller. It owns the pointer, the wheel, clicks and the keyboard, and its whole position is one number: the offset, in rows, fractional while it turns.
- Rows are stacked on the centre line and placed on the drum from there — out to the radius, `rotateX` by their distance from the offset, then the whole drum back by one radius so the front row sits on the screen plane at exactly one row high, under the highlight. Because they start centred rather than laid out down the column, a rotation has no layout offset to fight.
- The drum fills the column. The eye sits three radii in front of it, where its silhouette reaches `r · √(3/5)`; the radius is set so that equals half the column, and each row is a flat face of it (`step = 2 · atan(itemHeight / 2 / r)`). At the defaults that is `r = 116px`, a 17.6° step and a 348px perspective: the rows beside the centre stand at about 94%, 77%, 53% and 27% of their height and narrow as they roll back over the rim, and a fade darkens the surface toward it.
- Rows take no part in hit testing (`pointer-events: none`). The column reads the row under a point out of the projected geometry instead: a row turned by `a` is drawn at `y = r · sin a · 3 / (4 − cos a)`, which inverts in closed form, and points past the silhouette resolve to its rim. A transformed row's hit area travels with it, and the enlarged centre row would otherwise cover its neighbours and swallow their clicks.
- A drag tracks the finger, then coasts: the release velocity carries the offset on and it eases to the nearest enabled row on a cubic ease-out, so it leaves quickly and arrives slowly. The wheel turns the column directly and settles 120ms after it stops. With `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` a drag still follows the pointer, but there is no coast and the column lands on its row without easing.
- A controlled parent echoes every emitted value back through `modelValue`. A column already turning onto that value — easing there, or held by a drag or a wheel that committed it — is left to finish its turn; only a value the picker is not heading to re-places the column.
- Only the rows in front of the drum's rim are drawn — past `acos(1/4)` a row faces away from the eye and `backface-visibility` hides it. That is eleven rows at the default size, whatever the column's length. Each carries `aria-setsize` and `aria-posinset`, so the window is invisible to assistive tech.

## Technologies

- Source: `packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/picker/src/TxPicker.vue` defines the popup/inline rendering paths, normalization fallback, scroll snapping, `open` / `close` / `toggle` exposes, and row-size clamping.
- Type contracts: `packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/picker/src/types.ts` exports `PickerValue`, `PickerColumn`, `PickerOption`, `PickerProps`, and `PickerEmits`.
- **Verified coverage:** Coverage: `packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/picker/__tests__/picker.test.ts` covers value normalization, disabled-option fallback, toolbar confirm/cancel emissions, disabled toolbar/options, and clamped layout variables.
- Rejected: a fixed 18° step with a `9r` perspective and the front row pushed out toward the viewer. Only about ±36° of the drum fell inside a five-row column, the neighbours kept 95% of their height, the fade cut off everything past them, and the enlarged centre row overflowed the highlight — it read as a flat list sliding up and down.

